question:
The speed-time graph for a racing car is divided into four sections, P, Q, R and S. The car starts the race but soon crashes into a wall of tyres.
{{figure}}
Which sections of the graph show that there is an acceleration that is changing?

The diagram shows the four forces acting on an aircraft in flight.
{{figure}}
Which arrow shows the direction of the resultant of the four forces?

The diagrams show two metal blocks, X and Y, suspended from identical force meters. X and Y have identical dimensions.
{{figure}}
Which statement about X and Y is correct?

The diagrams E-H show a block of wood on a frictionless surface. In each diagram, the block has two forces acting on its sides.
{{figure}}
Which diagrams show the block in equilibrium?

A farmer has two carts. The carts have the same weight, but one has four narrow wheels and the other has four wide wheels.
{{figure}}
Which cart wheels sink less into soft ground and what is the reason?

The diagram shows two plane mirrors at 90° to each other. A ray of light is incident on one of the mirrors. The ray reflects off both mirrors before reaching a screen.
At which labelled point does the ray reach the screen?
{{figure}}

The diagram shows a bracelet containing two magnets. The arrows represent the pattern and the direction of the magnetic field due to the magnets.
{{figure}}
Which row identifies the magnetic pole at J, the magnetic pole at K and where the magnetic field is the strongest?

The circuits shown all include a d.c. power supply, one diode and two light-emitting diodes (LEDs).
In which circuit will both LEDs be turned on?
{{figure}}

A wire connected to a resistor \(\mathit{R}\) is moved in a magnetic field. A current is induced in the direction shown.
In which direction is the wire moved?
{{figure}}

There is a current in a straight metal wire in the direction shown.
{{figure}}
Which row describes the direction and the pattern of the magnetic field due to the wire when looking from vertically above the wire?

In an alpha particle scattering experiment, a beam of alpha particles is fired at a very thin piece of gold foil.
In which direction do most of the alpha particles travel after hitting the foil?
{{figure}}

The diagram shows a velocity-time graph for an object which is accelerating.
{{figure}}
What is the acceleration of the object?

Diagram 1 shows a piece of flexible material that contains many pockets of air. Diagram 2 shows the same piece of flexible material after it has been compressed so that its volume decreases.
{{figure}}
What happens to the mass and to the weight of the flexible material when it is compressed?

The diagram shows a glass flask sealed with a small volume of mercury in a glass tube. When the flask is gently warmed, the mercury rises up the tube.
{{figure}}
What is the main cause of the movement of the mercury?

Three solid copper spheres, X, Y and Z, are heated to the same temperature.
{{tbl:spherediametercolour of surfaceX\(\mathrm{2}\mathit{d}\)blackY\(\mathit{d}\)whiteZ\(\mathrm{2}\mathit{d}\)white}}
Which row gives the order for the rate of emission of radiation?

A small object O is placed near a converging lens, as shown. The lens forms an image I.
{{figure}}
Which statement is correct?

A student is trying to determine the resistance of a lamp. He sets up the incorrect circuit shown.
{{figure}}
Which change would allow him to take the measurements needed to calculate the resistance of the lamp?

The diagram shows the circuit for a potential divider.
{{figure}}
Which equation is used to calculate \({\mathit{V}}_{\mathrm{1}}\)?

A cell is connected to a parallel combination of a 2.0 Ω resistor and a 4.0 Ω resistor. The current in the 4.0 Ω resistor is 1.0 A.
{{figure}}
What is the current in the cell?

When there is an electric current in a long straight wire, a magnetic field is created around the wire.
Which diagram shows the correct pattern and direction of magnetic field lines around a long straight wire carrying current into the page?
{{figure}}

A car is travelling around a circular track at a constant speed, as shown.
In which direction is the resultant force on the car?
{{figure}}

The diagram shows some of the apparatus used to determine the specific heat capacity of a metal block.
{{figure}}
Which additional pieces of apparatus are required to find the specific heat capacity?

A piece of paper torn out of an exercise book is shown.
{{figure}}
What is being described?

The diagram shows one liquid floating on top of another liquid.
{{figure}}
Which statement explains why liquid P floats on top of liquid Q?

The diagram shows two narrow beams of light, P and then Q, passing through the same prism. Beams P and Q are both incident on the same point on the prism and at the same angle.
{{figure}}
Which row correctly compares beams P and Q?

The diagram shows part of the magnetic field around two magnets.
{{figure}}
Which list gives the order of magnetic field strengths at the positions P, Q and R, from weakest to strongest?

A student tries to predict the effect of exposure time on the radiation dose received from a source of ionising radiation. Radiation dose measures the amount of ionising radiation received by a living organism.
Which graph shows the correct trend between the variables?
{{figure}}

A force \(\mathit{F}\) is applied to a spanner, as shown.
{{figure}}
Which action increases the moment of \(\mathit{F}\) about the centre of the nut?

The diagram shows a simple a.c. generator.
{{figure}}
What is connected to G and H so that alternating current can be provided to an external circuit?

The diagrams show the coil in a d.c. electric motor in two positions. As the coil rotates through 180°, the direction of the current in the coil reverses from PQRS to SRQP.
{{figure}}
Which part of the motor is responsible for reversing the current?

The arrow shows the path of an \(\alpha \)-particle travelling towards the centre of a gold nucleus.
{{figure}}
Which description of the path of the \(\alpha \)-particle after striking the gold nucleus is correct?

Two beams of radiation, P and S, enter an electric field, as shown.
{{figure}}
Which types of radiation are P and S?

The diagram shows four labelled changes of state, P, Q, R and S, between solid, liquid and gas.
{{figure}}
Which changes need an energy input?

A scientist measures the air temperature at different heights from the floor in a cave. The results are recorded in the table.
{{tbl:height/mtemperature/°C0101011201330144016}}
Why does altering the height affect the temperature of the air?

The diagram shows a scale drawing of the formation of an image by the reflection of light from a plane mirror.
{{figure}}
What are the relationships between the labelled angles?

The diagram shows a human eye that correctly focuses the light on the retina.
{{figure}}
Which row shows a short-sighted eye and use of the correct lens to focus the image?

The diagram shows the magnetic field due to a current in a solenoid.
{{figure}}
Which graph represents the strength of the magnetic field at positions X, Y and Z?

The circuit diagrams show circuits that can control the potential difference (p.d.) across a lamp.
Which circuit allows the p.d. across the lamp to be varied from 0 V to 6.0 V?
